{
  "title": "39: al-Zumar الزمر",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nتَنْزِيْلُ الْكِتٰبِ مِنَ اللّٰهِ الْعَزِيْزِ الْحَكِيْمِ‏(1)\nTANZEELU KETAABE MENAL LAAHE A’ZEEZIL HAKEEM.\nThe revelation of this Book is from Allah, the Exalted in Power, full of Wisdom. \nاِنَّاۤ اَنْزَلْنَاۤ اِلَيْكَ الْكِتٰبَ بِالْحَقِّ فَاعْبُدِ اللّٰهَ مُخْلِصًا لَّهُ الدِّيْنَ ؕ‏(2)\nINNAA ANZALNAA ELAYKA KETAABA BIL-HAQQE FAAA’BUDE LAAHA MUKHLESAN LLAHU DEENA.\nVerily it is We Who have revealed the Book to thee in Truth: so serve Allah, offering Him sincere devotion. \nاَلَا لِلّٰهِ الدِّيْنُ الْخَالِصُ‌ ؕ وَالَّذِيْنَ اتَّخَذُوْا مِنْ دُوْنِهٖۤ اَوْلِيَآءَ‌ ۘ مَا نَعْبُدُهُمْ اِلَّا لِيُقَرِّبُوْنَاۤ اِلَى اللّٰهِ زُلْفٰى ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ يَحْكُمُ بَيْنَهُمْ فِىْ مَا هُمْ فِيْهِ يَخْتَلِفُوْنَ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يَهْدِىْ مَنْ هُوَ كٰذِبٌ كَفَّارٌ‏(3)\nALAA LILLAAHE DEENO AL-KHAALESU WAL LAZEENA ATTAKHAZOOA MIN DOONEHI AAWLEEAAAA MAA NAA’BUDUHUM ILLAA LEEQARREBOONAA ELAL LAAHE ZULFAA INNAL LAAHA YAHKOMO BAYNAHUM FEE MAA HUM FEEHE YAKHTALEFOON INNAL LAAHA LAA YAHDEE MAN HOWA KAAZEBUN KAFFAARUN.\nIs it not to Allah that sincere devotion is due? But those who take for protectors other than Allah (say): “We only serve them in order that they may bring us nearer to Allah.” Truly Allah will judge between them in that wherein they differ. But Allah guides not such as are false and ungrateful. \nلَوْ اَرَادَ اللّٰهُ اَنْ يَّتَّخِذَ وَلَدًا لَّاصْطَفٰى مِمَّا يَخْلُقُ مَا يَشَآءُ‌ ۙ سُبْحٰنَهٗ‌ ؕ هُوَ اللّٰهُ الْوَاحِدُ الْقَهَّارُ‏(4)\nLAW ARAADA LAAHO AN YYATTAKHEZA LAAHO LLAASTAFAA MIMMAA YAKHLOQO MAA YASHAAA WALADAN HOWA LAAHO AL-WAAHEDU AL-QAHHAARU.\nHad Allah wished to take to Himself a son, He could have chosen whom He pleased out of those whom He doth create: but Glory be to Him! (He is above such things.) He is Allah, the One, the Irresistible. \nخَلَقَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ بِالْحَقِّ‌ ۚ يُكَوِّرُ الَّيْلَ عَلَى النَّهَارِ وَيُكَوِّرُ النَّهَارَ عَلَى الَّيْلِ وَسَخَّرَ الشَّمْسَ وَالْقَمَرَ‌ؕ كُلٌّ يَّجْرِىْ لِاَجَلٍ مُّسَمًّى‌ؕ اَلَا هُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الْغَفَّارُ‏(5)\nKHALAQAL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA BIL-HAQQE YUKAWRU LAYLA A’LAL AN-NAHAARE WAYUKAWRU NAHAARA A’LAL LAYLE SAKHKHARASH SHAMSA WAL QAMARA KULLUL YYAJREAA LE-ELAA MOSAMMAA ALAA HOWA A’ZEEZUL AL-GHAFFAARU.\nHe created the heavens and the earth in true (proportions): He makes the Night overlap the Day, and the Day overlap the Night: He has subjected the sun and the moon (to His law): Each one follows a course for a time appointed. Is not He the Exalted in Power - He Who forgives again and again? \nخَلَقَكُمْ مِّنْ نَّفْسٍ وَّاحِدَةٍ ثُمَّ جَعَلَ مِنْهَا زَوْجَهَا وَاَنْزَلَ لَكُمْ مِّنَ الْاَنْعَامِ ثَمٰنِيَةَ اَزْوَاجٍ‌ ؕ يَخْلُقُكُمْ فِىْ بُطُوْنِ اُمَّهٰتِكُمْ خَلْقًا مِّنْۢ بَعْدِ خَلْقٍ فِىْ ظُلُمٰتٍ ثَلٰثٍ‌ ؕ ذٰ لِكُمُ اللّٰهُ رَبُّكُمْ لَهُ الْمُلْكُ‌ ؕ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ‌ ۚ فَاَ نّٰى تُصْرَفُوْنَ‏(6)\nKHALAQAKUM MIN NAFSIN WWAAHEDATIN SUMMA JA-A’LA MINHAA ZAWJAHAA WA ANZALA LAKUM MENAL AL-AANA’AAME SAMAANEETA AZWAAJINW YAKHLUQUKUM FEE BUTOONE MINHUNNA KHALQAN MIM BA’DE KHALQIN FEE ZOLOMAATIL SALAASIN ZAA LEKUMU LAAHO RABBOKUM LAHUL A’LAYNAA LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOWA FA-ANNAA TUSRAFOONA.\nHe created you (all) from a single person: then created, of like nature, his mate; and he sent down for you eight head of cattle in pairs: He makes you, in the wombs of your mothers, in stages, one after another, in three veils of darkness. such is Allah, your Lord and Cherisher: to Him belongs (all) dominion. There is no god but He: then how are ye turned away (from your true Centre)? \nاِنْ تَكْفُرُوْا فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ غَنِىٌّ عَنْكُمْ‌ وَلَا يَرْضٰى لِعِبَادِهِ الْكُفْرَ‌ ۚ وَاِنْ تَشْكُرُوْا يَرْضَهُ لَكُمْ‌ ؕ وَلَا تَزِرُ وَازِرَةٌ وِّزْرَ اُخْرٰى‌ ؕ ثُمَّ اِلٰى رَبِّكُمْ مَّرْجِعُكُمْ فَيُنَبِّئُكُمْ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‌ ؕ اِنَّهٗ عَلِيْمٌۢ بِذَاتِ الصُّدُوْرِ‏(7)\nIN TAKFUROOA FA-INNAL LAAHA GHANIYYUN A’NKUM WA LAA YARZAA LE-E’BAADEHIL KUFRA WA TASHKUROOA YARZAHU LAKUM WA LAA TAZERU WAAZERATUN WWEZRA LAHU SUMMA ELAA RABBEKUM MMARJEU’UKUM FAYONABBEOKUM BEMAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON INNAHU A’LEEM BE-ZAATIS SODOOR.\nIf ye reject (Allah), Truly Allah hath no need of you; but He liketh not ingratitude from His servants: if ye are grateful, He is pleased with you. No bearer of burdens can bear the burden of another. In the end, to your Lord is your Return, when He will tell you the truth of all that ye did (in this life). for He knoweth well all that is in (men's) hearts. \nوَاِذَا مَسَّ الْاِنْسَانَ ضُرٌّ دَعَا رَبَّهٗ مُنِيْبًا اِلَيْهِ ثُمَّ اِذَا خَوَّلَهٗ نِعْمَةً مِّنْهُ نَسِىَ مَا كَانَ يَدْعُوْۤا اِلَيْهِ مِنْ قَبْلُ وَجَعَلَ لِلّٰهِ اَنْدَادًا لِّيُضِلَّ عَنْ سَبِيْلِهٖ‌ ؕ قُلْ تَمَتَّعْ بِكُفْرِكَ قَلِيْلًا ‌ۖ  اِنَّكَ مِنْ اَصْحٰبِ النَّارِ‏(8)\nWA EZAA MASSAN INSAANA ZURRUN DA-A’A WAL MUNEEBAN ELAYHE SUMMA EZAA KHAWLAH NEA’MATAN MINHO NASEAAA MAA KAANA YAD-O’O ELAYHE MIN QABLO WA LILLAAHE ANDAADANW LLEEZELLA A’N SABEELEH QUL TAMATTAA’ BEKUFREKA QALEELAA INNAKA MIN ASHAABIL NAAR.\nWhen some trouble toucheth man, he crieth unto his Lord, turning to Him in repentance: but when He bestoweth a favour upon him as from Himself, (man) doth forget what he cried and prayed for before, and he doth set up rivals unto Allah, thus misleading others from Allah's Path. Say, “Enjoy thy blasphemy for a little while: verily thou art (one) of the Companions of the Fire!” \nاَمَّنْ هُوَ قَانِتٌ اٰنَآءَ الَّيْلِ سَاجِدًا وَّقَآئِمًا يَّحْذَرُ الْاٰخِرَةَ وَيَرْجُوْا رَحْمَةَ رَبِّهٖ‌ؕ قُلْ هَلْ يَسْتَوِى الَّذِيْنَ يَعْلَمُوْنَ وَالَّذِيْنَ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‌ؕ اِنَّمَا يَتَذَكَّرُ اُولُوا الْاَلْبَابِ‏(9)\nAMMAN HOWA QAANETUN AAANAAA LAYLE SAAJEDAN WWAQAAEMAN YYAHZARU AAKHERATA WA YARJOO RAHMATA RABBEH QUL HAL YASTAWEAA LAZEENA YA’LAMOON WAL LAZEENA LAA YAA’LAMOONA INNAMAA YATAZAKKARU ULUL ULIL ALBAABE.\nIs one who worships devoutly during the hour of the night prostrating himself or standing (in adoration), who takes heed of the Hereafter, and who places his hope in the Mercy of his Lord - (like one who does not)? Say: “Are those equal, those who know and those who do not know? It is those who are endued with understanding that receive admonition. \nقُلْ يٰعِبَادِ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوا اتَّقُوْا رَبَّكُمْ‌ ؕ لِلَّذِيْنَ اَحْسَنُوْا فِىْ هٰذِهِ الدُّنْيَا حَسَنَةٌ ‌ ؕ وَاَرْضُ اللّٰهِ وَاسِعَةٌ ‌ ؕ اِنَّمَا يُوَفَّى الصّٰبِرُوْنَ اَجْرَهُمْ بِغَيْرِ حِسَابٍ‏(10)\nQUL YAAE’EBAADE LAZEENA AAMANUT TAQOO TAQUL LILLAZEENA AAHSANOOA FEE HAAZEHE DUNYAA HASANATUL WAARZU LAAHE WAASE-A’TUN INNAMAA YOOFFAA SAABEROON AJRAHUM BEGHAYRIL HESAAB.\nSay: “O ye my servants who believe! Fear your Lord, good is (the reward) for those who do good in this world. Spacious is Allah's earth! those who patiently persevere will truly receive a reward without measure!” \nقُلْ اِنِّىْۤ اُمِرْتُ اَنْ اَعْبُدَ اللّٰهَ مُخْلِصًا لَّهُ الدِّيْنَۙ‏(11)\nQUL INNEE AN A-A’BODA AN HAAZEHIL BALDATIL LAAHA MUKHLESAN LLAHU DEENA.\nSay: “Verily, I am commanded to serve Allah with sincere devotion; \nوَاُمِرْتُ لِاَنْ اَكُوْنَ اَوَّلَ الْمُسْلِمِيْنَ‏(12)\nWA AN A-A’BODA LE-AN SHAY-IWN WA AWWALA AKOONA MENAL MUSLEMEEN.\n“And I am commanded to be the first of those who bow to Allah in Islam.” \nقُلْ اِنِّىْۤ اَخَافُ اِنْ عَصَيْتُ رَبِّىْ عَذَابَ يَوْمٍ عَظِيْمٍ‏(13)\nQUL INNEE AKHAAFO IN A’ASAYTU RABBEE A’ZAABAL YAWMIN A’ZEEM.\nSay: “I would, if I disobeyed my Lord, indeed have fear of the Penalty of a Mighty Day.” \nقُلِ اللّٰهَ اَعْبُدُ مُخْلِصًا لَّهٗ دِيْنِىۙ‏(14)\nQOLIL LAAHA A-A’BODUL MUKHLESAN LAHU DEENEAA.\nSay: “It is Allah I serve, with my sincere (and exclusive) devotion: \nفَاعْبُدُوْا مَا شِئْتُمْ مِّنْ دُوْنِهٖ‌ ؕ قُلْ اِنَّ الْخٰسِرِيْنَ الَّذِيْنَ خَسِرُوْۤا اَنْفُسَهُمْ وَ اَهْلِيْهِمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ‌ ؕ اَلَا ذٰ لِكَ هُوَ الْخُسْرَانُ الْمُبِيْنُ‏(15)\nFA BODOO MAA SHEATUM MIN DOONEHI QUL INNAL KHAASEREEN LAZEENA KHASEROOA ANFOSAHUM WA AHLEEHIM YAWMA QEYAAMATE ALAA ZAA LEKA HOWA AL-KHUSRAANU MOBEEN.\n“Serve ye what ye will besides him.” Say: “Truly, those in loss are those who lose their own souls and their People on the Day of Judgment: Ah! that is indeed the (real and) evident Loss! \nلَهُمْ مِّنْ فَوْقِهِمْ ظُلَلٌ مِّنَ النَّارِ وَمِنْ تَحْتِهِمْ ظُلَلٌ ‌ؕ ذٰ لِكَ يُخَوِّفُ اللّٰهُ بِهٖ عِبَادَهٗ‌ ؕ يٰعِبَادِ فَاتَّقُوْنِ‏(16)\nLAHUM MIN FAWQEHIM ZULALUN MENAL NAAR WA MIN TAHTEHEM ZULALUN ZAA LEKA YUKHAWFU LAAHO BEHI E’EBAADAH YAAE’EBAADE FAT-TAQOON.\nThey shall have Layers of Fire above them, and Layers (of Fire) below them: with this doth Allah warn off his servants: “O My Servants! then fear ye Me!” \nوَالَّذِيْنَ اجْتَنَبُوا الطَّاغُوْتَ اَنْ يَّعْبُدُوْهَا وَاَنَابُوْۤا اِلَى اللّٰهِ لَهُمُ الْبُشْرٰى‌ ۚ فَبَشِّرْ عِبَادِ ۙ‏(17)\nWAL LAZEENA AJTANABOOA AT-TAAGHOOTA AN YYAA’BUDOOHAA WAANAABOOA ELAL LAAHE LAHOMUL AL-BUSHRAA FABASSHER E’EBAADE.\nThose who eschew Evil, and fall not into its worship, and turn to Allah (in repentance), for them is Good News: so announce the Good News to My Servants, \nالَّذِيْنَ يَسْتَمِعُوْنَ الْقَوْلَ فَيَتَّبِعُوْنَ اَحْسَنَهٗ‌ ؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ هَدٰٮهُمُ اللّٰهُ‌ وَاُولٰٓئِكَ هُمْ اُولُوا الْاَلْبَابِ‏(18)\nLAZEENA YASTAMEU’OONA QAWLA FAYATTABEU’OONA AAHSANAH OOLAAA-EKA LAZEENA HADAAHUMU LAAHO WA OOLAAA-EKA HUM ULUL ULIL ALBAABE.\nThose who listen to the Word, and follow the best (meaning) in it: those are the ones whom Allah has guided, and those are the ones endued with understanding. \nاَفَمَنْ حَقَّ عَلَيْهِ كَلِمَةُ الْعَذَابِ ؕ اَفَاَنْتَ تُنْقِذُ مَنْ فِى النَّارِ‌ ۚ‏(19)\nAFAMAWN HAQQA A’LAYHE KALEMATU A’ZAABE AAFAANTA TUNQEZU MAN FIL NAAR.\nIs, then, one against whom the decree of Punishment is justly due (equal to one who eschews Evil)? Wouldst thou, then, deliver one (who is) in the Fire? \nلٰكِنِ الَّذِيْنَ اتَّقَوْا رَبَّهُمْ لَهُمْ غُرَفٌ مِّنْ فَوْقِهَا غُرَفٌ مَّبْنِيَّةٌ ۙ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ ؕوَعْدَ اللّٰهِ‌ ؕ لَا يُخْلِفُ اللّٰهُ الْمِيْعَادَ‏(20)\nLAAKENE LAZEENA TAQAW RABBAHUM LAHUM GHURAFUN MIN FAWQEHAA GHURAFUN MMABNEETUN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO WAA’DA LAAHE LAA YUKHLEFUL LAAHO AL-MEEA’AADA.\nBut it is for those who fear their Lord. That lofty mansions, one above another, have been built: beneath them flow rivers (of delight): (such is) the Promise of Allah: never doth Allah fail in (His) promise. \nاَلَمْ تَرَ اَنَّ اللّٰهَ اَنْزَلَ مِنَ السَّمَآءِ مَآءً فَسَلَكَهٗ يَنَابِيْعَ فِى الْاَرْضِ ثُمَّ يُخْرِجُ بِهٖ زَرْعًا مُّخْتَلِفًا اَ لْوَانُهٗ ثُمَّ يَهِيْجُ فَتَرٰٮهُ مُصْفَرًّا ثُمَّ يَجْعَلُهٗ حُطَامًا‌ ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَذِكْرٰى لِاُولِى الْاَلْبَابِ‏(21)\nALAM TARA ANNAL LAAHA ANZALAL MENAL SAMAAA-E MAAA-AN FASALAKAH YANAABEEA’A FIL ARZE SUMMA KHAB-A BEHI ZARA’AN MMUKHTALEFAN AALWAANUH SUMMA YAHEEJU FATARAAHU MUSFARRAL SUMMA YAJA’ALUH HOTAAMAN INNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LAZEKRAA LE-ULIL ULIL ALBAABE.\nSeest thou not that Allah sends down rain from the sky, and leads it through springs in the earth? Then He causes to grow, therewith, produce of various colours: then it withers; thou wilt see it grow yellow; then He makes it dry up and crumble away. Truly, in this, is a Message of remembrance to men of understanding. \nاَفَمَنْ شَرَحَ اللّٰهُ صَدْرَهٗ لِلْاِسْلَامِ فَهُوَ عَلٰى نُوْرٍ مِّنْ رَّبِّهٖ‌ؕ فَوَيْلٌ لِّلْقٰسِيَةِ قُلُوْبُهُمْ مِّنْ ذِكْرِ اللّٰهِ‌ؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ فِىْ ضَلٰلٍ مُّبِيْنٍ‏(22)\nAFAMAWN SHARAHA LAAHO SADRAH LIL-AESLAAME FAHOWA A’LAA NOORIN MIR RABBEH LAHUM LLELQAASEETE QULOOBUHUM MIN ELAA LAAH OOLAAA-EKA FEE ZALAALIM MOBEEN.\nIs one whose heart Allah has opened to Islam, so that he has received Enlightenment from Allah, (no better than one hard-hearted)? Woe to those whose hearts are hardened against celebrating the praises of Allah! they are manifestly wandering (in error)! \nاَللّٰهُ نَزَّلَ اَحْسَنَ الْحَدِيْثِ كِتٰبًا مُّتَشَابِهًا مَّثَانِىَ ‌ۖ  تَقْشَعِرُّ مِنْهُ جُلُوْدُ الَّذِيْنَ يَخْشَوْنَ رَبَّهُمْ‌ۚ ثُمَّ تَلِيْنُ جُلُوْدُهُمْ وَقُلُوْبُهُمْ اِلٰى ذِكْرِ اللّٰهِ‌ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ هُدَى اللّٰهِ يَهْدِىْ بِهٖ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ‌ ؕ وَمَنْ يُّضْلِلِ اللّٰهُ فَمَا لَهٗ مِنْ هَادٍ‏(23)\nALLAAHO NAZZALAL AHSANAL HAAZAL KETAABAA MMUTASHAABEHAN MMASAANEAAA TAQSHAE’ERRU MINHO JULOODU LAZEENA YAKHSHAWNA RABBAHUM SUMMA TALEENU JULOODUHUM WAQULOOBUHUM ELAA ELAA LAAHE ZAA LEKA HODAL LAAHE YAHDEE BEHI MAN YASHAAA-O WA MAN YYUZLELE LAAHO FAMAA LAHU MIN HAADIN.\nAllah has revealed (from time to time) the most beautiful Message in the form of a Book, consistent with itself, (yet) repeating (its teaching in various aspects): the skins of those who fear their Lord tremble thereat; then their skins and their hearts do soften to the celebration of Allah's praises. Such is the guidance of Allah: He guides therewith whom He pleases, but such as Allah leaves to stray, can have none to guide. \nاَ فَمَنْ يَّتَّقِىْ بِوَجْهِهٖ سُوْٓءَ الْعَذَابِ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ‌ ؕ وَقِيْلَ لِلظّٰلِمِيْنَ ذُوْقُوْا مَا كُنْتُمْ تَكْسِبُوْنَ‏(24)\nAFAMAWN YYATTAQEAA BE-WAJHEHI SOOO-AL A’ZAABE YAWMA QEYAAMATE WA QEELAD LIZ-ZAALEMEENA ZOOQOO MAA KUNTUM TAKSEBOONA.\nIs, then, one who has to fear the brunt of the Penalty on the Day of Judgment (and receive it) on his face, (like one guarded therefrom)? It will be said to the wrong-doers: “Taste ye (the fruits of) what ye earned!” \nكَذَّبَ الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ فَاَتٰٮهُمُ الْعَذَابُ مِنْ حَيْثُ لَا يَشْعُرُوْنَ‏(25)\nKAZZABA LAZEENA MIN QABLEHIM FA-ATAAHOMUL A’ZAABO MIN HAYSO LAA YASH-O’ROON.\nThose before them (also) rejected (revelation), and so the Punishment came to them from directions they did not perceive. \nفَاَذَاقَهُمُ اللّٰهُ الْخِزْىَ فِى الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا‌ ۚ وَلَعَذَابُ الْاٰخِرَةِ اَكْبَرُ‌ ۘ لَوْ كَانُوْا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(26)\nFAAZAAQAHUMU LAAHO AL-KHEZAAA FIL HAYAATID DUNYAA LA-A’ZAABUL AAKHERATE AKBARO LAW KAANOO YA’LAMOON.\nSo Allah gave them a taste of humiliation in the present life, but greater is the punishment of the Hereafter, if they only knew! \nوَلَقَدْ ضَرَبْنَا لِلنَّاسِ فِىْ هٰذَا الْقُرْاٰنِ مِنْ كُلِّ مَثَلٍ لَّعَلَّهُمْ يَتَذَكَّرُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(27)\nWA LAQAD ZARABNAA LIN-NAASE FEE HAAZAL QUR-AANE MIN KULLE MASALIN LA-A’LLAHUM YATAZAKKAROON.\nWe have put forth for men, in this Qur'an every kind of Parable, in order that they may receive admonition. \nقُرْاٰنًا عَرَبِيًّا غَيْرَ ذِىْ عِوَجٍ لَّعَلَّهُمْ يَتَّقُوْنَ‏(28)\nQURAANAN A’RABIYYAL GHAYRA ZEE E’EWAJIN LA-A’LLAHUM YATTAQOON.\n(It is) a Qur'an in Arabic, without any crookedness (therein): in order that they may guard against Evil. \nضَرَبَ اللّٰهُ مَثَلًا رَّجُلًا فِيْهِ شُرَكَآءُ مُتَشٰكِسُوْنَ وَرَجُلًا سَلَمًا لِّرَجُلٍ ؕ هَلْ يَسْتَوِيٰنِ مَثَلًا ‌ؕ اَلْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ ‌ ۚ بَلْ اَكْثَرُهُمْ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(29)\nZARABA LAAHO MASALAA RRAJULAN FEEHE SHURAKAAU MUTASHAAKESOONA WARAJULAN SALAMAN LLERAJULIN HAL YASTAWEENE MASALAA AALHAMDU LILLAAHE BAL AKSAROHUM LAA YA’LAMOON.\nAllah puts forth a Parable a man belonging to many partners at variance with each other, and a man belonging entirely to one master: are those two equal in comparison? Praise be to Allah! but most of them have no knowledge. \nاِنَّكَ مَيِّتٌ وَّاِنَّهُمْ مَّيِّتُوْنَ‏(30)\nINNAKA MAYTUN WWAANNAHUM MMAYTOONA.\nTruly thou wilt die (one day), and truly they (too) will die (one day). \nثُمَّ اِنَّكُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ عِنْدَ رَبِّكُمْ تَخْتَصِمُوْنَ‏(31)\nSUMMA INNAKUM YAWMA QEYAAMATE I’NDAL RABBEKUM TAKHTASEMOONA.\nIn the end will ye (all), on the Day of Judgment, settle your disputes in the presence of your Lord. \nفَمَنْ اَظْلَمُ مِمَّنْ كَذَبَ عَلَى اللّٰهِ وَكَذَّبَ بِالصِّدْقِ اِذْ جَآءَهٗ‌ ؕ اَ لَيْسَ فِىْ جَهَنَّمَ مَثْوًى لِّلْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(32)\nFAMAN AZLAMO MIMMAN KAZABA A’LAL LAAHE WA KAZZABA BEALSSEDQE IZ JAAA-AHU A-LAYSA FEE JAHANNAMA MASWAL LIL-KAAFEREEN.\nWho, then, doth more wrong than one who utters a lie concerning Allah, and rejects the Truth when it comes to him; is there not in Hell an abode for blasphemers? \nوَالَّذِىْ جَآءَ بِالصِّدْقِ وَصَدَّقَ بِهٖۤ‌ اُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الْمُتَّقُوْنَ‏(33)\nWAL LAZEE JAAA-A BEALSSEDQE WA SADDAQA BEHI OOLAAA-EKA HOMUL MUTTAQOON.\nAnd he who brings the Truth and he who confirms (and supports) it - such are the men who do right. \nلَهُمْ مَّا يَشَآءُوْنَ عِنْدَ رَبِّهِمْ‌ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ جَزٰٓؤُ الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ ۖۚ‏(34)\nLAHUM MAA YASHAAOONA I’NDAL RABBEHIM ZAA LEKA JAZAAAU MOHSENEEN.\nThey shall have all that they wish for, in the presence of their Lord: such is the reward of those who do good: \nلِيُكَفِّرَ اللّٰهُ عَنْهُمْ اَسْوَاَ الَّذِىْ عَمِلُوْا وَيَجْزِيَهُمْ اَجْرَهُمْ بِاَحْسَنِ الَّذِىْ كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(35)\nLEEKAFFERA LAAHO A’NHUM AASWAAALLAZEAA A’MELOO WAYAJZEEHUM AJRAHUM BE-AHSANE LAZEE KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nSo that Allah will turn off from them (even) the worst in their deeds and give them their reward according to the best of what they have done. \nاَلَيْسَ اللّٰهُ بِكَافٍ عَبْدَهٗ‌ ؕ وَيُخَوِّفُوْنَكَ بِالَّذِيْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِهٖ‌ ؕ وَمَنْ يُّضْلِلِ اللّٰهُ فَمَا لَهٗ مِنْ هَادٍ‌ ۚ‏(36)\nA-LAYSA LAAHO BEKAAFIN A’ABDAH WAYUKHAWFOONAKA BE-LAZEENA MIN DOONEHI WA MAN YYUZLELE LAAHO FAMAA LAHU MIN HAADIN.\nIs not Allah enough for his Servant? But they try to frighten thee with other (gods) besides Him! for such as Allah leaves to stray, there can be no guide. \nوَمَنْ يَّهْدِ اللّٰهُ فَمَا لَهٗ مِنْ مُّضِلٍّ‌ ؕ اَ لَيْسَ اللّٰهُ بِعَزِيْزٍ ذِى انتِقَامٍ‏(37)\nWA MAN YYAHDE LAAHO FAMAA LAHU MIM MMUZELLIN A-LAYSA LAAHO BEA’AZEEZIN ZIL ANTEQAAMIN.\nAnd such as Allah doth guide there can be none to lead astray. Is not Allah Exalted in Power, (Able to enforce His Will), Lord of Retribution? \nوَلَئِنْ سَاَ لْتَهُمْ مَّنْ خَلَقَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ لَيَقُوْلُنَّ اللّٰهُ‌ ؕ قُلْ اَفَرَءَيْتُمْ مَّا تَدْعُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ اِنْ اَرَادَنِىَ اللّٰهُ بِضُرٍّ هَلْ هُنَّ كٰشِفٰتُ ضُرِّهٖۤ اَوْ اَرَادَنِىْ بِرَحْمَةٍ هَلْ هُنَّ مُمْسِكٰتُ رَحْمَتِهٖ‌ ؕ قُلْ حَسْبِىَ اللّٰهُ‌ ؕ عَلَيْهِ يَتَوَكَّلُ الْمُتَوَكِّلُوْنَ‏(38)\nWA LAIN SA-ALTAHUM MAN KHALAQAL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA LAYAQOOLUNNAL LAAHO QUL AFA-RA-AYTUM MAA TADU’OONA MIN DOONIL LAAHE IN AARAADANEAAA LAAHO BEZURRIN HAL HUNNA KAASHEFAATU ZURREH AW AARAADANEAA BERAHMATIN HAL HUNNA MUMSEKAATU FEE QUL HASBEAAA LAAHO A’LAYHE YATAWAKKALU AL-MUTAWAKKELOONA.\nIf indeed thou ask them who it is that created the heavens and the earth, they would be sure to say, “Allah”. Say: “See ye then? the things that ye invoke besides Allah, can they, if Allah wills some Penalty for me, remove His Penalty? Or if He wills some Grace for me, can they keep back his Grace?” Say: “Sufficient is Allah for me! In Him trust those who put their trust.” \nقُلْ يٰقَوْمِ اعْمَلُوْا عَلٰى مَكَانَتِكُمْ اِنِّىْ عَامِلٌ‌ۚ فَسَوْفَ تَعْلَمُوْنَۙ‏(39)\nQUL LE-QAWMEHI AA’MALOOA A’LAA MAKAANATEKUM INNEE A’AAMELUN FA-SAWFA TA’LAMOON.\nSay: “O my People! Do whatever ye can: I will do (my part): but soon will ye know- \nمَنْ يَّاْتِيْهِ عَذَابٌ يُّخْزِيْهِ وَيَحِلُّ عَلَيْهِ عَذَابٌ مُّقِيْمٌ‏(40)\nMAN YYAATEEHE A’ZAABUN YYUKHZEEHE WA YAHILLO A’LAYHE A’ZAABUN MMUQEEMUN.\n“Who it is to whom comes a Penalty of ignominy, and on whom descends a Penalty that abides.” \nاِنَّاۤ اَنْزَلْنَا عَلَيْكَ الْكِتٰبَ لِلنَّاسِ بِالْحَقِّ‌ ۚ فَمَنِ اهْتَدٰى فَلِنَفْسِهٖ‌ ۚ وَمَنْ ضَلَّ فَاِنَّمَا يَضِلُّ عَلَيْهَا‌ ۚ وَمَاۤ اَنْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ بِوَكِيْلٍ‏(41)\nINNAA ANZALNAA A’LAYKAL KETAABA LIN-NAASE BIL-HAQQE FAMANE’ TADAA FALENAFSEH WA MAN ZALLA FA-INNAMAA YAZELLU A’LAYHAA WA MAA ANTA A’LAYHIM BEWAKEELIN.\nVerily We have revealed the Book to thee in Truth, for (instructing) mankind. He, then, that receives guidance benefits his own soul: but he that strays injures his own soul. Nor art thou set over them to dispose of their affairs. \nاَللّٰهُ يَتَوَفَّى الْاَنْفُسَ حِيْنَ مَوْتِهَا وَالَّتِىْ لَمْ تَمُتْ فِىْ مَنَامِهَا‌ ۚ فَيُمْسِكُ الَّتِىْ قَضٰى عَلَيْهَا الْمَوْتَ وَ يُرْسِلُ الْاُخْرٰٓى اِلٰٓى اَجَلٍ مُّسَمًّى‌ ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰیٰتٍ لِّقَوْمٍ يَّتَفَكَّرُوْنَ‏(42)\nALLAAHO YATAWAFFAA AL-AANFUSA HEENA MAWTEHAA WA LATEE LAM TAMUT FEE MANAAMEHAA FAYUMSEKU LATEE QAZAA A’LAYHAA MAWTA WA YURSELUR AL-AUKHRAAA ELAA ELAA AJALIM INNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LA-AAYAATIL LEQAWMINY YATAFAKKAROON.\nIt is Allah that takes the souls (of men) at death; and those that die not (He takes) during their sleep: those on whom He has passed the decree of death, He keeps back (from returning to life), but the rest He sends (to their bodies) for a term appointed verily in this are Signs for those who reflect. \nاَمِ اتَّخَذُوْا مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ شُفَعَآءَ‌ ؕ قُلْ اَوَلَوْ كَانُوْا لَا يَمْلِكُوْنَ شَيْئًا وَّلَا يَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(43)\nAMIL ATTAKHAZOOA MIN DOONIL LAAHE SHUFAA’AAA QUL LAW KAANOO LAA YAMLEKOONA SHAY-ANW WA LAA YA’QELOON.\nWhat! Do they take for intercessors others besides Allah? Say: “Even if they have no power whatever and no intelligence?” \nقُلْ لِّلَّهِ الشَّفَاعَةُ جَمِيْعًا‌ ؕ لَهٗ مُلْكُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ‌ ؕ ثُمَّ اِلَيْهِ تُرْجَعُوْنَ‏(44)\nQUL LILLAAH ASH-SHAFAAA’ATU JAMEE-A’A LAHU MULKUS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE SUMMA ELAYHE TURJA-O’ON.\nSay: “To Allah belongs exclusively (the right to grant) intercession: to Him belongs the dominion of the heavens and the earth: In the End, it is to Him that ye shall be brought back.” \nوَاِذَا ذُكِرَ اللّٰهُ وَحْدَهُ اشْمَاَزَّتْ قُلُوْبُ الَّذِيْنَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِالْاٰخِرَةِ‌ ۚ وَاِذَا ذُكِرَ الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِهٖۤ اِذَا هُمْ يَسْتَبْشِرُوْنَ‏(45)\nWA EZAA ZUKERA LAAHO WAHDAHU ASHMAAZZAT QULOOBU LAZEENA LAA YOAMENOONA BIL AAKHERATE WA EZAA ZUKERA LAZEENA MIN DOONEHI EZAA HUM YASTABSHEROON.\nWhen Allah, the One and Only, is mentioned, the hearts of those who believe not in the Hereafter are filled with disgust and horror; but when (gods) other than He are mentioned, behold, they are filled with joy! \nقُلِ اللّٰهُمَّ فَاطِرَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ عٰلِمَ الْغَيْبِ وَالشَّهَادَةِ اَنْتَ تَحْكُمُ بَيْنَ عِبَادِكَ فِىْ مَا كَانُوْا فِيْهِ يَخْتَلِفُوْنَ‏(46)\nQOLIL AL-LAAHUMMA FAATERA SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE A’AALEMA GHAYBE WASH SHAHAADATE ANTA TAHKUMU BAYNA E’BAADEKAS FEE MAA KAANOO FEEHE YAKHTALEFOON.\nSay: “O Allah! Creator of the heavens and the earth! Knower of all that is hidden and open! it is Thou that wilt judge between Thy Servants in those matters about which they have differed.” \nوَلَوْ اَنَّ لِلَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا مَا فِى الْاَرْضِ جَمِيْعًا وَّمِثْلَهٗ مَعَهٗ لَافْتَدَوْا بِهٖ مِنْ سُوْٓءِ الْعَذَابِ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ‌ؕ وَبَدَا لَهُمْ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ مَا لَمْ يَكُوْنُوْا يَحْتَسِبُوْنَ‏(47)\nWA LAW ANNAL LILLAZEENA ZALAMOO MAA FIL ARZE JAMEE-A’A WWAMESLAH MA-A’HU LAAFTADAWA BEHI MIN SOOE A’ZAABE YAWMA AL-QEEMATE WABADAA LAHUM MENAL LAAHE MAA LAM YAKOONOOA YAHTASEBOONA.\nEven if the wrong-doers had all that there is on earth, and as much more, (in vain) would they offer it for ransom from the pain of the Penalty on the Day of Judgment: but something will confront them from Allah, which they could never have counted upon! \nوَبَدَا لَهُمْ سَيِّاٰتُ مَا كَسَبُوْا وَحَاقَ بِهِمْ مَّا كَانُوْا بِهٖ يَسْتَهْزِءُوْنَ‏(48)\nWABADAA LAHUM SAYAAATU MAA KASABOO WAHAAQA BEHIM MAA KAANOO BEHI YASTAHZEOON.\nFor the evils of their Deeds will confront them, and they will be (completely) encircled by that which they used to mock at! \nفَاِذَا مَسَّ الْاِنْسَانَ ضُرٌّ دَعَانَا ثُمَّ اِذَا خَوَّلْنٰهُ نِعْمَةً مِّنَّا ۙ قَالَ اِنَّمَاۤ اُوْتِيْتُهٗ عَلٰى عِلْمٍ‌ؕ بَلْ هِىَ فِتْنَةٌ وَّلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَهُمْ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(49)\nFA-EZAA MASSAN INSAANA ZURRUN DAA’AANAA SUMMA EZAA KHAWLNAAHU NEA’MATAN MINNAA QAALA INNAMAA OOTEETOHU A’LAA E’ELMIN BAL HEYA FITNATUN WA LAAKINNA AKSARAHUM LAA YA’LAMOON.\nNow, when trouble touches man, he cries to Us: But when We bestow a favour upon him as from Ourselves, he says, “This has been given to me because of a certain knowledge (I have)!” Nay, but this is but a trial, but most of them understand not! \nقَدْ قَالَهَا الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ فَمَاۤ اَغْنٰى عَنْهُمْ مَّا كَانُوْا يَكْسِبُوْنَ‏(50)\nQAD QAALAHAA LAZEENA MIN QABLEHIM FAMAA AGHNAA A’NHUM MAA KAANOO YAKSEBOON.\nThus did the (generations) before them say! But all that they did was of no profit to them. \nفَاَصَابَهُمْ سَيِّاٰتُ مَا كَسَبُوْا‌ ؕ وَالَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا مِنْ هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ سَيُصِيْبُهُمْ سَيِّاٰتُ مَا كَسَبُوْا ۙ وَمَا هُمْ بِمُعْجِزِيْنَ‏(51)\nFAASAABAHUM SAYAAATU MAA KASABOO WAL LAZEENA ZALAMOO MIN HAAOOLAAA-E SAYUSEEBUHUM SAYAAATU MAA KASABOO WA MAA HUM BE-MO’JEZEENA.\nNay, the evil results of their Deeds overtook them. And the wrong-doers of this (generation)- the evil results of their Deeds will soon overtake them (too), and they will never be able to frustrate (Our Plan)! \nاَوَلَمْ يَعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّ اللّٰهَ يَبْسُطُ الرِّزْقَ لِمَنْ يَّشَآءُ وَيَقْدِرُ‌ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰلِكَ لَاٰيٰتٍ لِّقَوْمٍ يُّؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(52)\nAWALAM YAA’LAMOOA ANNAL LAAHA YABSOTUR RIZQA LEMAN-Y YASHAAA-O WA YAQDER INNAL FEE ZAALEKA LA-AAYAATIL LEQAWMINY YOAMENOON.\nKnow they not that Allah enlarges the provision or restricts it, for any He pleases? Verily, in this are Signs for those who believe! \nقُلْ يٰعِبَادِىَ الَّذِيْنَ اَسْرَفُوْا عَلٰٓى اَنْفُسِهِمْ لَا تَقْنَطُوْا مِنْ رَّحْمَةِ اللّٰهِ‌ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ يَغْفِرُ الذُّنُوْبَ جَمِيْعًا‌ ؕ اِنَّهٗ هُوَ الْغَفُوْرُ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(53)\nQUL YAA E’BAADEYAL LAZEENA AASRAFOOA A’LAA ANFOSEHIM LAA TAQNATOOA MIR RRAHMATE LAAHE INNAL LAAHA YAGHFERO AZ-ZUNOOBA JAMEE-A’A INNAHU HOWA GHAFOORUL RAHEEM.\nSay: “O my Servants who have transgressed against their souls! Despair not of the Mercy of Allah: for Allah forgives all sins: for He is Oft-Forgiving, Most Merciful. \nوَاَنِيْبُوْۤا اِلٰى رَبِّكُمْ وَاَسْلِمُوْا لَهٗ مِنْ قَبْلِ اَنْ يَّاْتِيَكُمُ الْعَذَابُ ثُمَّ لَا تُنْصَرُوْنَ‏(54)\nWAANEEBOOA ELAA RABBEKUM WAASLEMOOA LAHU MIN QABLE AN YAATEYAKOMUT A’ZAABO SUMMA LAA TUNSAROONA.\n“Turn ye to our Lord (in repentance) and bow to His (Will), before the Penalty comes on you: after that ye shall not be helped. \nوَاتَّبِعُوْۤا اَحْسَنَ مَاۤ اُنْزِلَ اِلَيْكُمْ مِّنْ رَّبِّكُمْ مِّنْ قَبْلِ اَنْ يَّاْتِيَكُمُ الْعَذَابُ بَغْتَةً وَّاَنْتُمْ لَا تَشْعُرُوْنَۙ‏(55)\nWA TABE-O’O AHSANAL MAA UNZELA ELAYKUM MIR RABBEKUM MIN QABLE AN YAATEYAKOMUT A’ZAABO BAGHTATANW WA ANTUL LAA TASH-O’ROON.\n“And follow the best of (the courses) revealed to you from your Lord, before the Penalty comes on you - of a sudden while ye perceive not!- \nاَنْ تَقُوْلَ نَفْسٌ يّٰحَسْرَتٰى عَلٰى مَا فَرَّطْتُّ فِىْ جَنْۢبِ اللّٰهِ وَاِنْ كُنْتُ لَمِنَ السّٰخِرِيْنَۙ‏(56)\nAN TAQOOLA NAFSUN YYAAHASRATAA A’LAA MAA FARRATTTU FEE JANBE LAAHE WA KUNTO LAMENAS AS-SAAKHEREENA.\n“Lest the soul should (then) say: 'Ah! Woe is me!- In that I neglected (my duty) towards Allah, and was but among those who mocked!'- \nاَوْ تَقُوْلَ لَوْ اَنَّ اللّٰهَ هَدٰٮنِىْ لَكُنْتُ مِنَ الْمُتَّقِيْنَۙ‏(57)\nAW TAQOOLA LAW ANNAL LAAHA HADAANEAA LAKUNTU MENAL MA-A’L MUTTAQEEN.\n“Or (lest) it should say: 'If only Allah had guided me, I should certainly have been among the righteous!'- \nاَوْ تَقُوْلَ حِيْنَ تَرَى الْعَذَابَ لَوْ اَنَّ لِىْ كَرَّةً فَاَكُوْنَ مِنَ الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(58)\nAW TAQOOLA HEENA TARAL A’ZAABA LAW ANNAL LEE KARRATAN FA SHAY-IWN WA MENAL MOHSENEEN.\n“Or (lest) it should say when it (actually) sees the penalty: 'If only I had another chance, I should certainly be among those who do good!' \nبَلٰى قَدْ جَآءَتْكَ اٰيٰتِىْ فَكَذَّبْتَ بِهَا وَاسْتَكْبَرْتَ وَكُنْتَ مِنَ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(59)\nBALAA QAD JAAATKA AAAYAATEAA FAKAZZABTA BEHAA WAASTAKBARTA WA KUNTA MENAL KAAFEREEN.\n“(The reply will be:) 'Nay, but there came to thee my Signs, and thou didst reject them: thou wast Haughty, and became one of those who reject faith!'“ \nوَيَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ تَرَى الَّذِيْنَ كَذَبُوْا عَلَى اللّٰهِ وُجُوْهُهُمْ مُّسْوَدَّةٌ ؕ اَلَيْسَ فِىْ جَهَنَّمَ مَثْوًى لِّلْمُتَكَبِّرِيْنَ‏(60)\nWA YAWMA QEYAAMATE TARAL LAZEENA KAZABOOA A’LAL LAAHE WOJOOHOHUM MMUSWADDATUN A-LAYSA FEE JAHANNAMA MASWAL LLELMUTAKABBEREENA.\nOn the Day of Judgment wilt thou see those who told lies against Allah;- their faces will be turned black; Is there not in Hell an abode for the Haughty? \nوَيُنَجِّىْ اللّٰهُ الَّذِيْنَ اتَّقَوْا بِمَفَازَتِهِمْ لَا يَمَسُّهُمُ السُّوْٓءُ وَلَا هُمْ يَحْزَنُوْنَ‏(61)\nWAYUNAJJEAA LAAHO LAZEENA TAQAW BEMAFAAZATEHEM LAA YAMASSUHUMU AS-SOOU WA LAA HUM HUM YAHZANOON.\nBut Allah will deliver the righteous to their place of salvation: no evil shall touch them, nor shall they grieve. \nاَللّٰهُ خَالِقُ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ‌ وَّ هُوَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ وَّكِيْلٌ‏(62)\nALLAAHO KHAALEQU KULLE SHAY-IN WA HOWA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN WWAKEELUN.\nAllah is the Creator of all things, and He is the Guardian and Disposer of all affairs. \nلَّهٗ مَقَالِيْدُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ‌ؕ وَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا بِاٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ اُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الْخٰسِرُوْنَ‏(63)\nLAHU MAQAALEEDU SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZ WAL LAZEENA KAFAROO BE-AAYAATIL LAAHE OOLAAA-EKA HOMUL KHAASEROON.\nTo Him belong the keys of the heavens and the earth: and those who reject the Signs of Allah, it is they who will be in loss. \nقُلْ اَفَغَيْرَ اللّٰهِ تَاْمُرُوْٓنِّىْۤ اَعْبُدُ اَيُّهَا الْجٰهِلُوْنَ‏(64)\nQUL AAFAGHAYRA LAAHE TAAMUROONNEAA A-A’BODUL AYYOHAL AL-JAAHELOONA.\nSay: “Is it some one other than Allah that ye order me to worship, O ye ignorant ones?” \nوَلَقَدْ اُوْحِىَ اِلَيْكَ وَاِلَى الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِكَ‌ۚ لَئِنْ اَشْرَكْتَ لَيَحْبَطَنَّ عَمَلُكَ وَلَتَكُوْنَنَّ مِنَ الْخٰسِرِيْنَ‏(65)\nWA LAQAD OOHEYA ELAYKA WA ELAL LAZEENA MIN QABLEKA LAIL AASHRAKTA LAYAHBATANNA A’AMALUKA WALATAKOONANNA MENAL KHAASEREEN.\nBut it has already been revealed to thee, as it was to those before thee, “If thou wert to join (gods with Allah), truly fruitless will be thy work (in life), and thou wilt surely be in the ranks of those who lose (all spiritual good)”. \nبَلِ اللّٰهَ فَاعْبُدْ وَكُنْ مِّنَ الشّٰكِرِيْنَ‏(66)\nBALIL LAAHA FAAA’BUD WA KUN MENAL ASH-SHAAKEREENA.\nNay, but worship Allah, and be of those who give thanks. \nوَمَا قَدَرُوْا اللّٰهَ حَقَّ قَدْرِهٖ ‌ۖ  وَالْاَرْضُ جَمِيْعًا قَبْضَتُهٗ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ وَالسَّمٰوٰتُ مَطْوِيّٰتٌۢ بِيَمِيْنِهٖ‌ ؕ سُبْحٰنَهٗ وَتَعٰلٰى عَمَّا يُشْرِكُوْنَ‏(67)\nWA MAA QADAROOA LAAHA HAQQA QADREH WAL JAMEE-A’A QABZATUH YAWMA QEYAAMATE WAALSSAMAAWAATU MATWEETUN BE-YAMEENEHI WALADAN TA-A’ALAA A’MMAA YUSHREKOON.\nNo just estimate have they made of Allah, such as is due to Him: On the Day of Judgment the whole of the earth will be but His handful, and the heavens will be rolled up in His right hand: Glory to Him! High is He above the Partners they attribute to Him! \nوَنُفِخَ فِى الصُّوْرِ فَصَعِقَ مَنْ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَنْ فِى الْاَرْضِ اِلَّا مَنْ شَآءَ اللّٰهُ‌ ؕ ثُمَّ نُفِخَ فِيْهِ اُخْرٰى فَاِذَا هُمْ قِيَامٌ يَّنْظُرُوْنَ‏(68)\nWA FIL SOORE FASAE’EQA MAN FIL SAMAAWAATE WA MAN FIL ARZE ILLAA MAN SHAAA-AL LAAHO SUMMA NUFEKHA FEEHE LAHU FA-EZAA HUM QEEAMUN YYANZUROONA.\nThe Trumpet will (just) be sounded, when all that are in the heavens and on earth will swoon, except such as it will please Allah (to exempt). Then will a second one be sounded, when, behold, they will be standing and looking on! \nوَاَشْرَقَتِ الْاَرْضُ بِنُوْرِ رَبِّهَا وَوُضِعَ الْكِتٰبُ وَجِآىْ ئَ بِالنَّبِيّٖنَ وَالشُّهَدَآءِ وَقُضِىَ بَيْنَهُمْ بِالْحَقِّ وَهُمْ لَا يُظْلَمُوْنَ‏(69)\nWAASHRAQATE ARZO BENOORE RABBEHAA WAWUZEA’A KETAABO WAJEAAAAA A BE-NABIYYEENA WA AN WA BAYNAHUM BIL-HAQQE WA HUM LAA LAA YUZLAMOON.\nAnd the Earth will shine with the Glory of its Lord: the Record (of Deeds) will be placed (open); the prophets and the witnesses will be brought forward and a just decision pronounced between them; and they will not be wronged (in the least). \nوَوُفِّيَتْ كُلُّ نَفْسٍ مَّا عَمِلَتْ وَهُوَ اَعْلَمُ بِمَا يَفْعَلُوْنَ‏(70)\nWAWUFFEET KULLO NAFSIM MAA A’MELAT WA HOWA A-A’LAMO BEMAA YAF-A’LOON.\nAnd to every soul will be paid in full (the fruit) of its Deeds; and (Allah) knoweth best all that they do. \nوَسِيْقَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْۤا اِلٰى جَهَنَّمَ زُمَرًا‌ ؕ حَتّٰٓى اِذَا جَآءُوْهَا فُتِحَتْ اَبْوَابُهَا وَقَالَ لَهُمْ خَزَنَتُهَاۤ اَلَمْ يَاْتِكُمْ رُسُلٌ مِّنْكُمْ يَتْلُوْنَ عَلَيْكُمْ اٰيٰتِ رَبِّكُمْ وَيُنْذِرُوْنَكُمْ لِقَآءَ يَوْمِكُمْ هٰذَا‌ ؕ قَالُوْا بَلٰى وَلٰكِنْ حَقَّتْ كَلِمَةُ الْعَذَابِ عَلَى الْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(71)\nWASEEQA LAZEENA KAFAROO ELAA JAHANNAMA ZUMARAN HATTAA EZAA JAAA-OOHAA FUTEHAT AABWAABUHAA WA QAALA LAHUM KHAZANATOHAA ALAM YAATEKUM RUSULUN MINKUM YATLOONAL A’LAYKUM AAYAATIL RABBEKUM WAYUNZEROONAKUM LE-QAAA-AL YAWMEKUM HAAZAA QAALOO BALAA WA LAAKIL HAQQAT KALEMATU A’ZAABE A’LAL KAAFEREEN.\nThe Unbelievers will be led to Hell in crowd: until, when they arrive, there, its gates will be opened. And its keepers will say, “Did not messengers come to you from among yourselves, rehearsing to you the Signs of your Lord, and warning you of the Meeting of This Day of yours?” The answer will be: “True: but the Decree of Punishment has been proved true against the Unbelievers!” \nقِيْلَ ادْخُلُوْۤا اَبْوَابَ جَهَنَّمَ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَا‌ۚ فَبِئْسَ مَثْوَى الْمُتَكَبِّرِيْنَ‏(72)\nQEELA KHOLOO AABWAABA JAHANNAMA KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA FA MASALUL MASWAA AL-MUTAKABBEREENA.\n(To them) will be said: “Enter ye the gates of Hell, to dwell therein: and evil is (this) Abode of the Arrogant!” \nوَسِيْقَ الَّذِيْنَ اتَّقَوْا رَبَّهُمْ اِلَى الْجَنَّةِ زُمَرًا‌ؕ حَتّٰٓى اِذَا جَآءُوْهَا وَفُتِحَتْ اَبْوَابُهَا وَقَالَ لَهُمْ خَزَنَتُهَا سَلٰمٌ عَلَيْكُمْ طِبْتُمْ فَادْخُلُوْهَا خٰلِدِيْنَ‏(73)\nWASEEQA LAZEENA TAQAW RABBAHUM ELAL JANNAH ZUMARAN HATTAA EZAA JAAA-OOHAA WAFUTEHAT AABWAABUHAA WA QAALA LAHUM KHAZANATOHAA SALAAMUN A’LAYKUM TEBTUM FAADKHULOOHAA KHAALEDEENA.\nAnd those who feared their Lord will be led to the Garden in crowds: until behold, they arrive there; its gates will be opened; and its keepers will say: “Peace be upon you! well have ye done! enter ye here, to dwell therein.” \nوَقَالُوا الْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الَّذِىْ صَدَقَنَا وَعْدَهٗ وَاَوْرَثَنَا الْاَرْضَ نَتَبَوَّاُ مِنَ الْجَنَّةِ حَيْثُ نَشَآءُ ‌ۚ فَنِعْمَ اَجْرُ الْعٰمِلِيْنَ‏(74)\nWA HAMDO LILLAAHE LAZEE SADAQANAA WA’DAHU WAAWRASANAA ARZA NATABAWAU MENAL JANNAH HAYSO NASHAAA-O FA NE’MA AJRUL A’AMELEENAL.\nThey will say: “Praise be to Allah, Who has truly fulfilled His Promise to us, and has given us (this) land in heritage: We can dwell in the Garden as we will: how excellent a reward for those who work (righteousness)!” \nوَتَرَى الْمَلٰٓئِكَةَ حَآفِّيْنَ مِنْ حَوْلِ الْعَرْشِ يُسَبِّحُوْنَ بِحَمْدِ رَبِّهِمْ‌ۚ وَقُضِىَ بَيْنَهُمْ بِالْحَقِّ وَقِيْلَ الْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ رَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(75)\nWA TARAL AL-MALAAAEKATA HAAFFEENA MIN HAWLE A’RSHIL YUSABBEHOONA BE-HAMDE RABBEHIM WA BAYNAHUM BIL-HAQQE WA QEELAD HAMDO LILLAAHE RABBIL A’ALAMEEN.\nAnd thou wilt see the angels surrounding the Throne (Divine) on all sides, singing Glory and Praise to their Lord. The Decision between them (at Judgment) will be in (perfect) justice, and the cry (on all sides) will be, “Praise be to Allah, the Lord of the Worlds!” ",
  "merits": "Surah al-Zumar (The Companies)\nThis Surah has 75 verses and it was revealed in Makkah. Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) said that whoever recites this Surah will be given a honourable and respectable status in this life and in the hereafter. Allah (s.w.t.) will give him so much respect in the eyes of the people that they will be in awe. The fire of Jahannam will be made haraam on his body (ie. he will never enter hell fire) and the gifts he will get in Jannah will be countless.\nThe Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) has said that is a person keeps this Surah (written) in his possession then whoever meets him will praise him. If this Surah is tied to one’s arm then whoever sees him will praise him."
}
